error[type.method]: `.type(…)` interns into its receiver, and `int` has no `interned`
  ╭─[<case>/src/main.av:2:1]
2 │ r.type(int)
  · ┬
  · ╰── written here
──╯
  `r.type(int)` asks the receiver to fold the type, spelled as a value, into its id
help: declare `interned` on `int` — its seat is the enum the literal spells, its answer the id — or name a table that has one: `cx.type(…)`
